# Binary assets must never have their line endings rewritten.
#
# This repo is cloned on Windows with core.autocrlf=true. Git guesses text-vs-binary by looking
# for NUL bytes near the start of a file, and some PDFs — the reportlab-generated lead magnets
# in assets/downloads/ among them — have none, so Git classified them as TEXT and warned it
# would convert LF to CRLF on checkout. That silently corrupts the file: the committed blob is
# fine, but a fresh clone writes a broken PDF, and these are files people download.
#
# Marking the types explicitly removes the guesswork.
*.pdf   binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.webp  binary
*.ico   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary
*.zip   binary
*.docx  binary
*.xlsx  binary
*.mp4   binary

# Keep the web sources normalised in the repo regardless of who commits them.
*.html  text
*.css   text
*.js    text
*.mjs   text
*.json  text
*.md    text
*.py    text
*.svg   text
*.xml   text
*.txt   text
